@inject UserSession Session

<div class="help-article">
    <p class="help-lead">
        Keep the receipt with the claim. <a href="receipts/scan">Scan receipt</a> photographs a paper receipt, reads its total,
        date and store, finds the transaction it belongs to and attaches it, so the proof is there when you file.
    </p>

    <h3>Scanning a receipt</h3>
    <ol>
        <li><strong>The receipt.</strong> <span class="help-ui">Use camera</span> on a computer with a webcam or on a phone; lay the receipt flat
            in good light and fill the frame. Or <span class="help-ui">Send from phone</span> to show a QR code, scan it with your
            phone's camera and take the photo there. Or choose a photo or PDF you already have.</li>
        <li><strong>What it says.</strong> As soon as the photo is in, LoonieBooks reads the <span class="help-ui">Total</span>,
            <span class="help-ui">Date</span> and <span class="help-ui">Store</span> in your browser; the photo isn't sent anywhere to be
            read. Correct anything it got wrong and the matches update.</li>
        <li><strong>The transaction it belongs to.</strong> This step appears once there's a photo. LoonieBooks lists the spending that
            fits the receipt and picks a clear winner for you; choose another if it's wrong. If none fits, use
            <span class="help-ui">Not one of these? Search your transactions</span> (shown straight away when nothing matches) to look
            by dates, amount and description. Optionally choose a tax category under <span class="help-ui">Also claim it as</span>,
            then attach it.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="help-note">
        Some setups also offer <span class="help-ui">Read with Claude</span> for receipts the browser struggles with. That one
        <em>does</em> send the photo to Anthropic's API to be read, so it's only used when you press it.
    </p>

    <h3>Attaching from the tax report</h3>
    <p>
        Every claim on the <a href="tax">Tax report</a> has its own attach button: choose a PDF or photo up to 5 MB. Attached
        receipts are listed under the transaction, where you can download one or remove it with ✕. Confirmed claims without one
        are counted in the <strong>Missing receipts</strong> tile and marked <em>missing</em> on the printable summary.
    </p>

    <h3>Where receipts are kept</h3>
    <p>
        @if (Session.Storage == StorageLocation.Browser)
        {
            @:With your ledger, in this browser. They're part of
        }
        else if (Session.IsDesktop)
        {
            @:With your ledger, in LoonieBooks' database on the computer running it. They're part of
        }
        else
        {
            @:With your ledger, in this server's database. They're part of
        }
        <a href="data">backups</a>, and they go if the transaction is removed by undoing its import.
    </p>
</div>
